// ---- spq-preop-functions (SPQ-020) [option-gated] ----
// CompiledStep(..., pre_op=f) / async_pre_op=f where f names a function of the same file that runs imperative
// execution: it calls one of the runtime names (preop_seeds) or, transitively, a function of the file that does.
// Generated by /tmp/w03/gen_spq-preop-functions.py from the clause JSON (inputs through tr.py, projections by hand).
// Inputs: spq_preop_functions_<input>(n) are the nodes each input's rule + file block match (tr.py), in in-scope parsing documents.
//   Projections: capture.NAME = text of the def's `name` child (spq_preop_functions_fn_name); capture.CALLEE = text of the call's
//   identifier function or its attribute's `attribute` (spq_preop_functions_callee); capture.VALUE (each) = text of the
//   identifier value of each pre_op= / async_pre_op= keyword argument (spq_preop_functions_step_value). All three captures are
//   identifiers, so the projected capture text is text(): exact (no string decoding / value() involved).
// Stage imperative = spq_preop_functions_imperative(d, name): the recursive CTE as Datalog recursion over the file's finite
//   (d, name, callee) call edges (spq_preop_functions_calls_in); the CTE's UNION is set semantics, as Datalog's.
// The query = the violation rule; key (issue, identity = call start) collapses to the call node; line = its line.
// partitionBy file / requireNonemptyInput admission: spq_preop_functions_admitted(d), per document [INFERENCE: per-file admission].
// Exactness notes:
// - `c.__start > f.__start AND c.__end <= f.__end` is read as `inside(c, f, function_definition)` (strict ancestor):
//   tree spans nest, and no call starts where a function_definition starts.
// - preop_steps' `has(has(keyword_argument))` through `arguments`: the keyword argument is a named child of the
//   argument list; child() leaves out comments only, which are never keyword arguments: exact.
// Reads node_text (the module-text regexes pre_op / CompiledStep of the admission and `inside module` tests).
.decl spq_preop_functions_kinds0(kind: symbol)
spq_preop_functions_kinds0("module").
.decl spq_preop_functions_kinds1(kind: symbol)
spq_preop_functions_kinds1("function_definition").
