// ---- spq-vector-filter-constants (SPQ-042): a QueryFilter column given as a module constant naming branch_id/revision_id -------
// Relational clause, partitionBy file, in impl/common/l2070_server_plan/steps/intent_vector_query.py only.
// Inputs (W matchers, translated by tr.py, `syntax: valid`, in scope):
//   spq_vector_filter_constants_filter_names(n)    filter_names: an identifier that is QueryFilter(...)'s first positional argument (nthChild
//                          1 ofRule: not a keyword_argument / list_splat / dictionary_splat; exact, ofRule leaves
//                          comments out) or its `column=` keyword value; row spq_vector_filter_constants_fn(d, n, name = its text);
//   spq_vector_filter_constants_module_strings(s)  module_strings: a module-level `NAME = <string>` (no annotation; a plain, raw or
//                          unicode string, or a concatenation without interpolation or f-string part); row
//                          spq_vector_filter_constants_ms(d, s, NAME, DECODED);
//   spq_vector_filter_constants_admission(n)       admission: the module, when its text matches QueryFilter (requireNonemptyInput, per
//                          file: spq_vector_filter_constants_admitted(d)).
// DECODED is `replace` over `$STRING` with `value: true` and the never-matching regex \b\B: the right-hand
// string's value (W's `value`, not followed, as Python's str()), i.e. value(string, v) (escapes decoded, adjacent
// literals joined). Not modelled: where W cannot know that value it fails the clause (transform-fact-failure,
// demand/driver/catalog/sql_backend.rs), and a clause failure has no .rr form. It does not arise for the literals
// the input admits (a str literal with an [rRuU]* prefix, or a concatenation of those), which W decodes, short of
// W's value budget (rr's value has none): past it W fails the clause where this reports.
// Stage module_string_values = spq_vector_filter_constants_last (the max __start module_strings row per (path, NAME),
// taken over every module_strings row, valued or not). Query:
// filter_names rows with a module_string_values row of the same path and name whose value is 'branch_id' or
// 'revision_id'. Key (issue, identity = n.__start): one finding per identifier, at its line.
// Otherwise exact (the inputs are their matchers rule for rule). Reads node_text (the module `regex` gate QueryFilter and the string
// prefix regexes (?i)^[ru]*['"] / (?i)^(?:fr|rf|f)['"], W's whole node text) and value.
// Option-gated: the inputs' `file` blocks read entryPoint / oracleAnalyzer (option_value, option_on).
